[00:13.50] With quill and silver knife
[00:21.06] She carved a poison pen
[00:28.83] Wrote to her lover's wife
[00:36.77] "Your husband's seed has fed my flesh"
[00:44.82] As if a leper's face
[00:52.75] That tainted letter graced
[01:00.95] The wife with choke-stone throat
[01:08.58] Ran to the day with tear-blind eyes
[03:21.97] Impaled on nails of ice
[03:29.46] And raked o'er emerald fire
[03:37.17] The wife with soul of snow
[03:44.86] With steady hand, begins to write
[03:52.82] "I'm still, I need no life
[04:01.01] To serve on boys and men
[04:09.15] What's mine was yours is dead
[04:17.14] I take my leave of mortal flesh"
[04:24.28] 